{
  // Blocking SCA gate for the Expo / React Native mobile app (npm lockfile).
  // Fails CI on high/critical advisories. See docs/SUPPLY_CHAIN.md.
  //
  // Runtime vs. development dependencies:
  //   - PRODUCTION deps (react-native, @react-navigation/*, expo-* — the code
  //     actually bundled onto the device by EAS/Expo) carry NO high/critical
  //     advisory. A new high/critical in a shipped dependency MUST fail this job.
  //   - The allowlisted advisories below are all in code that runs on a
  //     developer's or EAS build machine, never inside the Metro bundle
  //     installed on a device. Each documents why no bump clears it.
  //
  // brace-expansion is NOT allowlisted: it is forced to 5.0.12 via a blanket
  // npm `override` in package.json. 5.0.10 and 5.0.11 are the patched versions
  // for the two stack-exhaustion advisories (GHSA-6j4f-fj2g-mc7p and
  // GHSA-qhr7-859c-m2p7, both high, published 2026-09-29), which supersede the
  // earlier GHSA-3jxr-9vmj-r5cp / GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg pair the override was
  // first added for. serve-handler's minimatch@3 still tolerates the 5.x export
  // shape because our rewrite patterns contain no braces, so expand() is never
  // invoked. The uuid moderate sits below this high+ gate. Keep the allowlist
  // minimal so a genuinely new high/critical still fails the job.
  //
  // Each exception documents owner + reason + review date. Prune an entry once
  // its dependency is bumped past the patched version.
  "high": true,
  "allowlist": [
    // (GHSA-5xrq-8626-4rwp pruned 2026-10-31: vitest is now 4.1.12, outside its
    // <=3.2.5 range — the vitest 4 upgrade that replaced Renovate's #825.)
    // (GHSA-fx2h-pf6j-xcff pruned 2026-10-24: the blanket vite override to
    // 6.4.4 — added for GHSA-587h-7wmj-h5pm — is past its <=6.4.2 range.)
    // (GHSA-86w9-cpqp-85rv pruned 2026-10-31: node-forge is now 1.4.2, outside its
    // <=1.4.0 range — the bump that cleared the five 2026-10-30 node-forge highs.)
    // owner: security@kube-coder | review: 2026-10-03 | build-time only, NO FIX PUBLISHED
    //
    // braces <=3.0.3 exhausts the stack on a deeply nested pattern.
    // first_patched_version is null — 3.0.3 is the newest release and is
    // itself in range, so no bump clears this. Published 2026-09-18, but it
    // began failing this job on 2026-10-02 when the affected range widened
    // to include 3.0.3, which is why it appeared on every branch at once
    // rather than with any one change.
    //
    // Reachable only through the Metro bundler's own file-map
    // (metro > metro-file-map > micromatch > braces, plus the same path via
    // @expo/metro and @react-native/community-cli-plugin). Metro runs on the
    // developer or EAS build machine over this repo's own glob patterns; it
    // is not in the bundle shipped to a device, and no attacker-supplied
    // pattern reaches it. A DoS against our own build is a failed build.
    //
    // Re-check when braces publishes a patched line, or when Metro moves off
    // micromatch.
    "GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm", // braces <=3.0.3  stack exhaustion via nested patterns — no patch exists
    // owner: security@kube-coder | review: 2026-10-24 | build-time only, fix is a major @expo/cli can't take
    //
    // zod <4.6.6 can exhaust memory validating oversized constrained
    // collections. The only patched line is 4.6.6+; @expo/cli pins zod ^3
    // (3.25.76 here), so no in-range bump clears it and an npm override to
    // zod 4 would break the Expo CLI's own schemas.
    //
    // Reachable only through `expo` > `@expo/cli`, which runs on the
    // developer/EAS build machine parsing this repo's own config — it is not
    // in the Metro bundle shipped to a device, and no attacker-supplied input
    // reaches its validators. A DoS against our own build is a failed build.
    //
    // Re-check when @expo/cli moves to zod 4 (Expo SDK 58 is expected to),
    // or if zod backports the fix to a 3.x release.
    "GHSA-mrhx-c7xc-m3w5"  // zod <4.6.6  memory exhaustion on oversized constrained collections — fix only in 4.x
  ],
  "report-type": "summary"
}
